  "narrative": "No assessments are due and independent validation is exhausted, so this explore stage registers discovery-only refinements targeting the main remaining dataset-specific uncertainty: the architecture of the feature_010 context dependence and the robustness of the accepted feature_002, feature_003, feature_063, feature_037, and signature axes. The central supported pattern is that feature_037 is strongly associated with lower outcome_001, feature_002 is associated with higher outcome_001, feature_003 lowering is localized mainly to higher feature_036, feature_063 lowering is context-dependent, and feature_010 is non-monotone: positive overall and in many low contexts, but lower outcome_001 in high or nonnegative feature_038 and feature_018 clean contexts. The first proposal asks whether the accepted high-high feature_010 lowering remains when feature_037 and feature_002 are both absent, which tests dependence on the dominant feature_037 and residual feature_002 axes. The second proposal tests whether feature_038 modifies the feature_010 contrast after removing feature_037 and feature_002. The next two proposals reverse earlier feature_010 lowering claims in feature_002-positive feature_018 or feature_038 contexts because the signed lower-claim estimates were negative, implying an opposite raw positive association; these are new changed-direction claims linked to their parents. The feature_010 proposal at feature_018 <= 0 tests the complementary low-signature context within feature_002-positive observations. The feature_002 proposals test whether the accepted positive higher-outcome residual axis persists in a lower feature_008 assay context and in an older feature_019 observed stratum. The feature_003 proposals test whether localized lowering persists in higher feature_036 after removing feature_037 and feature_002, and whether it is reinforced in a nonnegative feature_018 setting. The feature_063 proposal tests whether lowering persists after removing feature_037 and feature_002. These are unadjusted Welch contrasts in the supplied dataset, judged against the 0.15 composite dependency-score-unit threshold in the claimed direction. All estimates returned later are already signed to the registered direction. These analyses do not support causality, biological mechanism, gene or pathway identity, single-gene knockout biology, coding correctness, or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 20 explore corrected: validation budget remains exhausted. Accepted dataset-specific architecture: feature_037 dominant lowering; feature_002 strong positive higher-outcome residual; feature_010 context dependent, positive overall and in many low or feature_002-positive contexts but lowering in high or nonnegative feature_038/feature_018 clean contexts; feature_003 lowering localized mainly to higher feature_036; feature_063 lowering context dependent. New proposals refine feature_010 clean high-high lowering, feature_038 interaction among clean feature_037=0 feature_002=0 observations, reversed direct feature_010 claims in feature_002-positive contexts where prior lowering claims were opposite, feature_010 positive in feature_002-positive low feature_018, feature_002 robustness in lower feature_008 and older feature_019, feature_003 high feature_036 with feature_037 and feature_002 absent and with nonnegative feature_018, and feature_063 lowering after removing feature_037 and feature_002. Parent links use available displayed evidence. Main unresolved: precise feature_010 reversal architecture independent of feature_002 and feature_037, feature_063 localization boundaries, feature_003 in clean feature_002/feature_037 contexts, conditioning and collider risk, high multiplicity. All claims remain unadjusted associations in the supplied dataset only."
